 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# M2→M3: From Gradient Descent to Multi-Layer Networks\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**Act 1 (M2):** Where do gradients come from? Define a single neuron in sympy,\\n",
    "differentiate symbolically, lambdify into numpy, and run gradient descent by hand.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**Act 2 (M3):** Connect multiple neurons, trust backpropagation, and use the\\n",
    "pipeline's `NumpyModel` + `CrossEntropyLoss` to train a real MLP on Titanic.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**Prerequisites:** `pip install sympy matplotlib pandas`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Act 1 (M2): A Single Neuron's Gradient"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import sympy as sp\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Define symbols\\n",
    "w, b, x, t = sp.symbols('w b x t')\\n",
    "# Single neuron: y = sigmoid(w*x + b)\\n",
    "y = 1 / (1 + sp.exp(-(w*x + b)))\\n",
    "# MSE loss: L = (y - t)^2\\n",
    "L = (y - t)**2\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Symbolic gradients\\n",
    "dL_dw = sp.diff(L, w)\\n",
    "dL_db = sp.diff(L, b)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"dL/dw =\\", sp.simplify(dL_dw))\\n",
    "print(\\"dL/db =\\", sp.simplify(dL_db))"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Lambdify into numpy functions\\n",
    "grad_w_fn = sp.lambdify([w, b, x, t], dL_dw, 'numpy')\\n",
    "grad_b_fn = sp.lambdify([w, b, x, t], dL_db, 'numpy')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Test on one data point\\n",
    "w_val, b_val = 0.5, 0.0\\n",
    "x_val, t_val = 1.0, 0.0\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(f\\"grad_w = {grad_w_fn(w_val, b_val, x_val, t_val):.6f}\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"grad_b = {grad_b_fn(w_val, b_val, x_val, t_val):.6f}\\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\\n",
    "from pipeline.adapters.numpy_adapter import NumpyModel, NumpyOptimizer\\n",
    "from pipeline.training.optimizers import SGD\\n",
    "from pipeline.protocols import Parameter\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Initialize parameters (single neuron)\\n",
    "W_data = np.array([[0.5]])\\n",
    "b_data = np.array([0.0])\\n",
    "model = NumpyModel([(W_data, b_data)], activation=\\"relu\\")\\n",
    "opt = NumpyOptimizer(model.parameters(), SGD(lr=0.1))\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Training data: y = 2x\\n",
    "X = np.array([[1.0], [2.0], [3.0], [4.0]])\\n",
    "y = np.array([[2.0], [4.0], [6.0], [8.0]])\\n",
    "\\n",
    "losses = []\\n",
    "for epoch in range(50):\\n",
    "    epoch_loss = 0\\n",
    "    for i in range(len(X)):\\n",
    "        x_i = X[i:i+1]\\n",
    "        y_i = y[i:i+1]\\n",
    "        pred = model.forward(x_i)\\n",
    "        loss_val = float(np.mean((pred - y_i)**2))\\n",
    "        epoch_loss += loss_val\\n",
    "\\n",
    "        # Manual gradient: dL/dpred = 2*(pred - y_i)\\n",
    "        dL_dpred = 2 * (pred - y_i)\\n",
    "        model.backward(dL_dpred)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "        opt.step()\\n",
    "        opt.zero_grad()\\n",
    "\\n",
    "    losses.append(epoch_loss / len(X))\\n",
    "\\n",
    "params = list(model.parameters())\\n",
    "print(f\\"Final loss: {losses[-1]:.6f}\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Learned W: {params[0].data[0,0]:.4f} (target: 2.0)\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Learned b: {params[1].data[0]:.4f} (target: 0.0)\\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n",
    "plt.plot(losses)\\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\\"Epoch\\")\\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\\"MSE Loss\\")\\n",
    "plt.title(\\"Single Neuron: Gradient Descent from First Principles\\")\\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**What we just did:** Derived gradient formulas by hand (sympy), converted to numpy\\n",
    "(lambdify), ran gradient descent manually, verified the neuron learned y = 2x.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**Now:** Let's do the same for a multi-layer network on Titanic — but let\\n",
    "backpropagation handle the gradients."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Act 2 (M3): Multi-Layer Network on Titanic"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\\n",
    "import pandas as pd\\n",
    "\\n",
    "from pipeline.config import Config\\n",
    "from pipeline.data.csv_source import CsvDataSource\\n",
    "from pipeline.data.split import train_test_split\\n",
    "from pipeline.evaluation.metrics import Metrics, accuracy\\n",
    "from pipeline.hooks.progress import ProgressHook\\n",
    "from pipeline.pipeline import BasePipeline, PipelineState\\n",
    "from pipeline.adapters.numpy_adapter import NumpyModel, NumpyOptimizer\\n",
    "from pipeline.training.losses import CrossEntropyLoss\\n",
    "from pipeline.training.optimizers import Adam\\n",
    "\\n",
    "config = Config(\\n",
    "    data_dir=\\"./data/titanic\\",\\n",
    "    output_dir=\\"./outputs/m3-numpy\\",\\n",
    "    batch_size=32,\\n",
    "    num_epochs=100,\\n",
    "    train_ratio=0.8,\\n",
    "    learning_rate=0.01,\\n",
    "    seed=42,\\n",
    "    task_name=\\"titanic-numpy-mlp\\",\\n",
    ")\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"Configuration ready\\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "class TitanicNumpyMLP(BasePipeline):\\n",
    "    \\"\\"\\"Two-layer numpy MLP on Titanic.\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "\\n",
    "    def load_data(self, state):\\n",
    "        source = CsvDataSource(\\n",
    "            \\"data/titanic/train.csv\\",\\n",
    "            batch_size=config.batch_size,\\n",
    "            target_column=\\"Survived\\",\\n",
    "            shuffle=True,\\n",
    "            seed=config.seed,\\n",
    "        )\\n",
    "        train, val = train_test_split(source, train_ratio=config.train_ratio)\\n",
    "        state.data_stream = train\\n",
    "        state.val_data_stream = val\\n",
    "\\n",
    "    def build_model(self, state):\\n",
    "        rng = np.random.default_rng(config.seed)\\n",
    "        # 7 input features → 16 hidden → 2 output classes\\n",
    "        W1 = rng.standard_normal((16, 7)) * np.sqrt(2.0 / 7)\\n",
    "        b1 = np.zeros(16)\\n",
    "        W2 = rng.standard_normal((2, 16)) * np.sqrt(2.0 / 16)\\n",
    "        b2 = np.zeros(2)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "        state.model = NumpyModel([(W1, b1), (W2, b2)], activation=\\"relu\\")\\n",
    "        state.loss_fn = CrossEntropyLoss(model=state.model)\\n",
    "        state.optimizer = NumpyOptimizer(\\n",
    "            state.model.parameters(),\\n",
    "            Adam(lr=config.learning_rate),\\n",
    "        )\\n",
    "        state.metrics = Metrics(accuracy=accuracy)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "    def evaluate(self, state):\\n",
    "        state.model.eval_mode()\\n",
    "        preds, trues = [], []\\n",
    "        for batch in state.val_data_stream:\\n",
    "            logits = np.asarray(state.model.forward(batch.inputs))\\n",
    "            preds.append(np.argmax(logits, axis=1))\\n",
    "            trues.append(np.asarray(batch.targets))\\n",
    "        y_pred = np.concatenate(preds)\\n",
    "        y_true = np.concatenate(trues)\\n",
    "        state.metrics.compute(y_true, y_pred)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "    def export(self, state):\\n",
    "        state.predictions = np.array([0])\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"Pipeline class defined\\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "pipeline = TitanicNumpyMLP(config)\\n",
    "pipeline.add_hook(ProgressHook())\\n",
    "state = pipeline.run(\\"train\\")\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(f\\"\\\\nAccuracy: {state.metrics['accuracy']:.4f}\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Final loss: {state.history['loss'][-1]:.4f}\\")\\n",
    "print(\\"Training complete!\\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Compare: M1 (sklearn) vs M3 (numpy MLP)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "| | M1 sklearn | M3 numpy MLP |\\n",
    "|---|---|---|\\n",
    "| Model | LogisticRegression | 2-layer MLP (7→16→2) |\\n",
    "| Training | `.fit()` one call | 100 epochs per-batch GD |\\n",
    "| Optimizer | LBFGS (internal) | Adam (lr=0.01) |\\n",
    "| Loss | log-loss (internal) | CrossEntropyLoss |\\n",
    "| Parameters | None exposed | 4 Parameters (W1,b1,W2,b2) |\\n",
    "| Gradient | sklearn internal | manual backprop in `model.backward()` |\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**Key insight:** The same pipeline structure ran both. The sklearn path overrode\\n",
    "`train()`; the numpy path used the default `TrainLoop`. The protocol design works."
   ]
  }
